# Marine

## Lore

These soldiers follow the ancient traditions of the US Marine Corps and bear the insignia and colours of that branch of service. Marines were trained to operate in the air, at sea and on land, with a particular accent on amphibious combat. The pre-Rifts USS Ticonderoga carried an entire division of them, and those troops became the core of the New Marine Corps.

Marines serve aboard every ship in the New Navy and provide security for all its land installations, including the Salvation and Refuge Bases and cities.

## GM Notes

The current crop of jarheads - a pre-Rifts slang term that has survived into the New Navy - has been bloodied against everything from human outlaws and pirates to transdimensional monsters. Their training covers things the Marines of the twentieth century would never have imagined, such as monster identification and resistance to mind control.

They are equipped with advanced weapons and armour from the automated factories at the Salvation and Refuge Bases. That equipment was cutting-edge before the Rifts, and only the best products of Triax, the Splugorth and Naruni Enterprises surpass it.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'marine');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'marine';
SELECT count(*) AS stub_gear FROM gear WHERE slug IN ('marine-combat-armor', 'm-2011-pistol', 'm-160-assault-rifle');

